# ─── Old VDP slug patterns (CarsForSale-era) — added 2026-06-29, Leo ──
# Search Console "Not found (404)" report (June 2026) surfaced ~163 dead
# URLs. The bulk are legacy auto-CMS vehicle-detail pages plus a stray
# /default — never mapped at cutover, so they hard-404 and waste whatever
# Google equity they still hold. 301 to /inventory/ so equity consolidates
# and the legacy URLs deindex cleanly. Patterns confirmed from the live GSC
# 404 export: /Inventory/Details/{guid}, /default, /inventory/{brand}/{model}/{stock}.

# Legacy VDP detail pages: /Inventory/Details/{guid}
/Inventory/Details/*         /inventory/                       301
/inventory/details/*         /inventory/                       301

# Stray legacy homepage alias
/default                     /                                 301
/default/                    /                                 301

# Old brand/model/stock VDP format: /inventory/{brand}/{model}/{stock}
# e.g. /inventory/lexus/rc/11266. Live VDPs are single-segment
# (/inventory/{slug}/), so this 3-segment pattern cannot collide with a
# live car page or with the :slug rewrite below.
/inventory/:brand/:model/:stock   /inventory/                  301

# ─── GSC 404 sweep round 2 (2026-07-28, Leo) ────────────────────────
# The 2026-06-29 pass (3d31c39) matched only the NO-trailing-slash form
# of the legacy VDP pattern. Google has these indexed WITH the slash, so
# /inventory/acura/mdx/11248/ still hard-404'd while the bare form 301'd.
#
# !! HARD-LEARNED LIMIT (measured live 2026-07-28) !!
# Cloudflare's docs claim 2,000 static + 100 dynamic redirects. The REAL
# behaviour on this project is that everything past roughly the 114th
# rule is SILENTLY IGNORED - no build error, no warning, the rules just
# never fire. A first pass at this fix shipped 230 rules; rules 1-114
# worked and 115-230 did nothing. Probed every rule live to find the
# edge. KEEP THE TOTAL RULE COUNT UNDER ~100 and re-probe after any
# bulk addition. Prefer exact static rules for known-bad URLs over
# speculative wildcard coverage - splats are dynamic and scarce.
#
# Placeholder rules match PER SEGMENT, so the 2- and 3-segment forms
# below can never collide with a live VDP, which is always ONE segment
# under /inventory/. Bare make pages (/inventory/lexus/) ARE one segment,
# so they are enumerated explicitly instead of pattern-matched.

# Legacy 3-segment VDP - trailing-slash form (the half 3d31c39 missed)
/inventory/:brand/:model/:stock/               /inventory/            301
# !! DO NOT add 2-segment /inventory/:a/:b wildcard rules — EVER.
# Next.js client navigation fetches /inventory/<slug>/index.txt and
# /inventory/<slug>/__next._tree.txt. Both are 2-segment paths, so a
# 2-segment wildcard 301s them to /inventory/ and EVERY vehicle click
# on the whole site bounces back to the inventory list (live outage
# 2026-07-28 -> 2026-07-30, introduced by 3164b89, removed here).
# Legacy 2-segment make/model URLs get EXACT static rules only.

# Bare legacy make index under /inventory/ (must be explicit - see above)
/inventory/acura/                              /brands/acura/         301
/inventory/honda/                              /brands/honda/         301
/inventory/lexus/                              /brands/lexus/         301
/inventory/mazda/                              /brands/mazda/         301
/inventory/subaru/                             /brands/subaru/        301
/inventory/toyota/                             /brands/toyota/        301

